# Episode scripts

When writing plot or `scripts_input/` JSON, follow **Episode script authoring** and the JSON schema in `PLAN.md`. Do not invent a different schema.

- Read `characters/*.json` and `locations/*.json` first. Use only those `id`s. Location JSON is the set bible; the empty plate PNG is generated by `content:frames`, not copied from a character still.
- Every scene has `characterIds` and `locationId`. Same room across shots = same `locationId`, never a new prose description of the set.
- `imagePrompt`: shot only (size, camera height, pose, lips, props already in frame). No motion, no speech, no set-dressing (that lives on the location).
- `videoPrompt`: cinematographer shot list — shot size, one present-tense action, camera (static or slow push), timed speech, matching foley, **no music**. Do not re-describe wardrobe or architecture.
- Speech: short quoted lines, two beats max, lips slightly parted in the still, prop in frame if she handles it. No clenched-jaw CUs, no “looks past the camera,” no off-screen voices.
- One speaker. No crowds, fights, morphs, 360s, on-screen text, mid-clip location/wardrobe/face changes.
- Size `durationSeconds` to the line + one action.
- Reply with valid episode JSON only (no markdown fences) unless the human asked for a plan first.
